Committee Secretary: Good morning.

24
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:47,880
Committee Secretary: I think that is all for now, Mr. Chair.

25
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:52,340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Committee Secretary.

26
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:57,340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

27
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:07,680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As we begin our deliberations on the proposed budget or budgets of the Movie and Television Review and Classification Board,

28
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:14,040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: the Optical Media Board, the Film Development Council of the Philippines, and the Philippine Racing Commission,

29
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:21,580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'd like to emphasize that these agencies may appear to operate in very different fields,

30
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:27,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: but they share one important responsibility, protecting the public,

31
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:34,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: interests while supporting industries that contribute to our economy, culture, and livelihood of our people.

32
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:38,640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ang budget po ng pamahalaan ay pera po ng taong bayan.

33
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:39,800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We all know that.

34
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:43,540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya sa bawat pisong ilalaan natin sa mga ahensya ninyo,

35
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:51,260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: dapat malinaw kung saan ito gagamitin, ano ang kongkretong resulta, at paano makikinabang ang ating mga kababayan.

36
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:56,140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Let's tackle, first, the budget of the MTRCB.

37
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For MTRCB, we have...

38
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:05,960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For MTRCB, the agency was given under 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 75.29 million pesos.

39
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:14,500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 49.99 million.

40
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:22,620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Today, Filipinos are consuming content not only through traditional television and cinema,

41
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:26,900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: but also through streaming platforms and various digital channels.

42
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:33,140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Our children, in particular, have unprecedented access to content.

43
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:38,320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We, therefore, need to ask whether a regulatory framework is keeping pace with these changes.

44
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:02,880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Second, the Optical Media Board.

45
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:11,020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For OMB, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 47.03 million.

46
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:18,740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 53.462 million.

47
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:23,200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The media landscape has dramatically changed.

48
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: CDs and DVDs...

49
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:36,140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We have moved into a digital environment where content can be copied, downloaded, distributed, streamed, and reproduced almost instantly.

50
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: This raises an important question.

51
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:46,300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is the Optical Media Board still operating with the mandate and systems appropriate for today's digital economy?

52
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:50,540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We need to make sure that public funds are being used efficiently,

53
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:57,080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: that the agency is responding to actual threats to intellectual property and legitimate businesses.

54
00:07:57,660 --> 00:08:01,200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Third, the Film Development Council of the Philippines.

55
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:11,900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For FDCP, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act, a total budget of 367.35 million pesos.

56
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:19,460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 311.74.

57
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:23,880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The Philippine film industry is not merely an entertainment industry.

58
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:27,200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It is part of our cultural identity.

59
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:34,880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It is also a potential source of jobs, tourism, investment, and international recognition for Filipino talent.

60
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:44,740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We have Filipino filmmakers, actors, writers, directors, animators, cinematographers, editors, production workers, and other creative professionals

61
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:49,720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: who have demonstrated that we can compete internationally.

62
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:56,620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: But government support must translate into real opportunities for Filipino workers and filmmakers.

63
00:08:57,240 --> 00:09:03,340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We should therefore examine how FDCP's program are benefiting independent filmmakers,

64
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:11,580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: regional filmmakers, young artists, and emerging talents that only establish names in the industry.

65
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Finally, the Philippine Racing Commission or FILRACOM.

66
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:21,580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For FILRACOM, the agency was given under the 2026 General Appropriations Act,

67
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:26,580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: a total budget of 199.76 million pesos.

68
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:34,040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027, it is requesting a total budget of 202.85 million pesos.

69
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:38,440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The horse racing industry is not simply about betting or entertainment.

70
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:47,200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It involves breeders, trainers, jockeys, veterinarians, farm workers, racetrack employees,

71
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:51,500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and thousands of families whose livelihoods are connected to the industry.

72
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:55,600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ibig sabihin po, nakapagbibigay po siya ng trabaho.

73
00:09:55,600 --> 00:10:00,020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We therefore need to ensure that FILRACOM is effectively regulating the industry,

74
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:03,740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: protecting the integrity of horse racing,

75
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:11,520
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and making sure that the government revenues generated from the sector are properly accounted for and maximized.

76
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:18,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would therefore like to know whether FILRACOM proposed budget is sufficient to strengthen regulation,

77
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: improving monitoring, modernize its system,

78
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:28,400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and ensure transparency in the collection and utilization of racing revenues.

79
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:33,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: These four agencies operate in different sectors, but they face a common challenge.

80
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:38,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The world is changing faster than our regulatory and support systems.

81
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:43,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Horse racing is becoming more technologically driven.

82
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:47,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Media piracy is becoming increasingly digital.

83
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:52,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Television and film consumption are moving toward online platforms.

84
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:58,400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And the creative economy is becoming increasingly global.

85
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:04,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Therefore, our budget deliberation should not simply ask how much money does the agency need.

86
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:08,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We should ask more important questions like,

87
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:15,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: what will the Filipino people get in return for the budget given to you?

88
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:19,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Every allocation must have a corresponding public benefit.

89
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:24,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We need stronger accountability, measurable outcomes, efficient use of resources,

90
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:32,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and programs that directly benefit Filipino workers, consumers, artists, and entrepreneurs.

91
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:36,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At the end of the day, ang budget po ay hindi lamang numero sa papel,

92
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:41,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: buhay, trabaho at serbisyo publiko ang nakasalalay dito.

93
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:47,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya ngayong deliberasyon, I look forward to hearing from your agencies,

94
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:53,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: your respective offices, their concrete plans, their accomplishments, their challenges,

95
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:58,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and most importantly, how they intend to ensure that every peso entrusted to them

96
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:02,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: by the Filipino people will be put to good use.

97
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:04,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Maraming salamat po.

98
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:21,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay, on that note, let us proceed with the briefing proper.

99
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For the orderly procedure,

100
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:26,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: we will have the following chronology of budget presentation.

101
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:30,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: First to present is the Movie and Television Review Classification Board,

102
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:35,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: MTRCB, followed by the OMB Optical Media Board,

103
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: then the Film Development Council of the Philippines,

104
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:41,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and last, the Philippine Racing Commission, or FILRACOM.

105
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:44,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We will open the floor for queries or questions

106
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:48,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: after each presentation of the aforementioned agencies.

107
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:51,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We now recognize Chairperson Lala Soto Antonio

108
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:57,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: for the presentation of MTRCB's proposed budget for Fiscal Year 2027.

109
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:00,480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ma'am, please proceed with your presentation.

110
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Senator Erwin Tulfo, thank you.

111
