MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: comprises 27% of the total budget

129
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: that is sourced from the national government.

130
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:15,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The remaining 73% for the maintenance

131
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:19,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: and other operating expenses and the capital outlay

132
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: amounting to $144.51 million

133
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:26,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: again is sourced from the agencies' collected income.

134
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:30,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The graph shows the proposed budget

135
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:34,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for Fiscal Year 2027 by appropriation source

136
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:39,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: with a total of $197,898,000.

137
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:43,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agencies specific for personal services

138
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:46,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: amounting to $49.99 million

139
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: comprises the 25.1 million

140
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:51,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: and 25.26% of the total budget,

141
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:55,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: while the 1.72% of which will be

142
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:59,480
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: for the retirement and life insurance premium

143
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,400
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: GSIS.

144
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:19,020
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The remaining 73.02% will be sourced in the Special Account in the General Fund or the Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses and the Capital Outlay amounting to 144.51 million.

145
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:39,020
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For 2027, the total proposed budget for Capital Outlay amounts to 35.78 million allocated for ICT software and equipment or the year-to-implementation of the redevelopment of a transact and collection system of the MTRCB.

146
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:48,760
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: As of July 31, 2026, the book balance of our sinking fund amounts to

147
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:58,700
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: 641,412,719.08 centavos.

148
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:16,820
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For the budget utilization rate, from 2020 to 2025, the MTRCB steadily improved its budget utilization with obligation rates rising from 70.23% in 2020

149
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:23,390
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: to a peak of 97.72% in 2023,

150
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:44,300
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Before settling at 95.31% in 2024 and 86.92% in 2025, disbursement efficiency has also strengthened, reaching 93.16% in 2025, underscoring effective fund release and program execution.

151
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:57,700
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agency received significantly larger allotment of 267.67 million.

152
00:16:57,700 --> 00:17:09,040
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Of this, 110,175,000 has been obligated, reflecting a 41.16% obligation rate.

153
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:18,720
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Disbursement remains strong at 98.68 million, or 89.57%, sustaining the MTRCB.

154
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:23,840
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The agency's record of efficient fund release once obligations are made.

155
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:37,420
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: This mid-year performance highlights continued strength in disbursement efficiency, with obligations expected to accelerate in the latter half of the year, to align with the increased allocation.

156
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:47,960
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: For the financial performance, fiscal year 2025, the table shows the financial performance of the MTRCB for 2025.

157
00:17:48,720 --> 00:18:10,220
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: From 176.06 million, allotment received 86.93%, or 153.05 million of it was obligated, and 93.17% or 143.59 million was disbursed for fiscal year 2025.

158
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:18,720
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The unobligated allotment, amounting to 22.419 million, was moved as a continuing allocation.

159
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:32,100
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The unpaid obligations, amounting to 10.459 million, was recorded as accounts payable and paid during the first quarter of fiscal year 2025.

160
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:41,840
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The table above shows the financial performance of the MTRCB as of June 30, 2026.

161
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:47,740
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: From the 267.67 million allotment received,

162
00:18:48,720 --> 00:19:04,880
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: 41.16% or 110.175 million of it was obligated, and an 89.57% or 98.68 million was disbursed for the first half of 2026.

163
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:15,500
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: The unobligated allotment, amounting to 157.495 million, was scheduled for the third and fourth quarters of the year.

164
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,500
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: With a target to earn 96%.

165
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:22,460
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: With a target to earn 96 million worth of revenue for fiscal year 2025,

166
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:38,260
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: I'm happy to share, Mr. Chairman, we attained 130.46%, or an equivalent of 125.224 million total revenue as of December 31, 2025.

167
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:47,460
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: In fiscal year 2025, review fees accounted for the majority of our revenue at 77.26%.

168
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:58,060
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Followed by registration fees at 13.06% and miscellaneous income at 9.41%.

169
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:11,440
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: Revenue collection in January to June 2025 reached 67.97 million, achieving 70.80% of the 96 million target.

170
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:18,400
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: In January to June 2026, despite a higher target of 98 million,

171
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:34,260
MTRCB Chairperson Diorella Maria ?Lala? Sotto-Antonio: collections declined to 62 points, a 5.36 million decrease in actual collections,

